From 6f7a66e1ea537fc54035e753a7bbdbfa3a25fcc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:35:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Now-playing dashboard: full-height portrait, sharp art, new
 type

The first layout stretched a 512 px cover across a TV and used the stock font. The
portrait now fills the left half of the screen edge to edge and fades into the
background, with the album cover as a thumbnail on it. The text, lyrics and timeline take
the right half. The picture is requested at the image proxy's 1024 size so it stays
sharp, and the lyrics viewer, which is sized for a full screen, is scaled to the column.

Titles use Syne and the rest Outfit, both embedded as Latin subsets (SIL OFL 1.1) so a
TV needs no download. The size helper comes with tests first.
